benchmarks/subset/ulr_vs_upl -- the 100 programs of [2] Ultimate-LR vs Ultimate-PL for --subset
===================================================================================================

The programs on which scripts/run_full_evaluation.sh --subset runs [2], with the paper's 1000 s
timeout per run. The files are unchanged copies of programs of benchmarks/ulr_vs_upl (Figure 6).

How they were chosen (benchmarks/subset/select_subsets.py, from logs/results_ULR_vs_UPL.csv): the
benchmark's classes in its proportions -- solved by both runs (terminating, non-terminating), by
Ultimate-PL only, by Ultimate-LR only, by neither. The programs neither run solves are taken among
those both runs give up on within 60 s, to keep the subset short. The draws use
random.Random(seed) for seed = 1, 2, ...; the first one whose time differences reproduce those of
the whole benchmark within the bounds below is kept: seed 280. A uniform draw does not: most of
the gain of Ultimate-PL comes from a few long programs, and on short programs it is a few percent
slower, as each call to PaSTTeL costs a new process.

                                           subset  benchmark   bounds
    terminating, Ultimate-PL vs -LR        -11.3%      -9.9%   [-13.9%, -5.9%]
    non-terminating, Ultimate-PL vs -LR      +2.8%      +5.0%   [+1.0%, +9.0%]
    total (Cumulative Intersection)         -7.4%      -5.4%   [-7.9%, -2.9%]
    terminating gain, in noise std          -2.8               [-, -2]
    total gain, in noise std                -2.4               [-, -2]
    running time, both runs                  1.5h              [-, 2.5h]
    solved: Ultimate-LR / Ultimate-PL    82 / 84    891 / 911 

"In noise std" is the gain divided by the run-to-run noise it accumulates: 0.15 times each
program's Ultimate-LR time, the spread of (Ultimate-PL - Ultimate-LR) / Ultimate-LR between our run
and a rerun of 60 programs on another machine. Below -2, the gain should show on any machine.
As in the whole benchmark, where the 10 largest gains make 83 % of all the gains,
one program carries most of the subset's gain (-81 s): b.07-alloca_false-no-overflow.c, 89 s with
Ultimate-LR and 11 s with Ultimate-PL (-79 s), a gap far beyond the noise.

The columns give our result for each program (logs/ULR_vs_UPL_logs.zip, timeout 1000 s per run):
the verdict of each run, its wall clock, and the program's class.

